# A run of nouns hides how each noun relates to the next (`the state
# snapshot format upgrade logic`), and the reader has to guess which
# noun modifies which. Four nouns in a row is past the three-noun
# limit the technical-writing skill sets. The tagger marks some
# adjectives and verbs as nouns, and a heading or table cell often
# names a thing with a noun string on purpose, so the rule is a
# suggestion.
expr main [(NOUN NOUN NOUN NOUN)]
let message "Noun cluster. Break it up with `of`, `for`, or a relative clause."
let description "Flags four nouns in a row, which hide how each noun relates to the next."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The release notes branch is protected."
